      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَلُوكٌ</span></b>  <i>A thing that is eaten</i> [or rather <i>chewed,</i>
as will be seen below]: so in the phrases,
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هذَا أَلُوكُ صِدْقٍ</span> like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَلُوجُ صِدْقٍ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَلُوكُ صِدْقٍ</span>
[<i>This is an excellent thing that is chewed</i>], and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا تَلَوَّكْتُ بِأَلُوكٍ </span> [or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِأَلُوكٍ</span> ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا تَأَلَّكْتُ</span></b>  (K in art.

